==================== Input ====================
# Bail-out 3, at the edge where the merge tag is not spelled `!!merge`.
#
# `%TAG` can bind any handle to `tag:yaml.org,2002:`, and this parser stores directives
# uninterpreted, so a literal match on `!!merge` misses `!m!merge`. That is not cosmetic: two merge
# keys have order-dependent precedence, so missing one changes the document's merged value. Verified
# with `yaml@2`: before this refusal, the output below parsed with `q: 9` instead of `q: 1`.
%TAG !m! tag:yaml.org,2002:
---
openapi: 3.0.0
content:
  zz: 1
  !m!merge B: { q: 1 }
  !m!merge A: { q: 9 }
  aa: 3

